From 7f455a222d1923fca09b2bd6897037f447e65b7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Zheng <bluevisor@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:31:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Tracker: Quick Look on the space bar

Space previews the selected entry in a floating window, like Quick Look
in the macOS Finder: images scaled to fit, text files in a scrollable
monospace view, anything else as a large icon with name, kind, size and
modification date. The window avoids focus, so arrow keys keep moving
the selection and the preview follows; space or Escape close it. It
zooms out of the selected icon on open and back into it on close,
showing a scaled snapshot of its content during the animation.

Space still extends type-ahead while a name is being typed. Not used in
file panels.
